  {
    "id": "5524dc7ddeb08b422f96ae27",
    "path": "datafusion_common::tree_node::TreeNodeRecursion::Jump",
    "name": "Jump",
    "owner": "datafusion_common::tree_node::TreeNodeRecursion",
    "crate": "datafusion-common",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "variant",
    "signature": "Jump",
    "docs": "In top-down traversals, skip recursing into children but continue with\nthe next node, which actually means pruning of the subtree.\n\nIn bottom-up traversals, bypass calling bottom-up closures till the next\nleaf node.\n\nIn combined traversals, if it is the `f_down` (pre-order) phase, execution\n\"jumps\" to the next `f_up` (post-order) phase by shortcutting its children.\nIf it is the `f_up` (post-order) phase, execution \"jumps\" to the next `f_down`\n(pre-order) phase by shortcutting its parent nodes until the first parent node\nhaving unvisited children path.",
